queue_evidence, envelope_by_id)` with `return None`.

Result RED: `python3 -m unittest
tests.test_auth_envelope.TestEnvelopePresenceGating` →
`Ran 11 tests, FAILED (failures=5)` — identical count to log R1. Failing
set observed: `test_clean_landing_without_envelope_stalls_when_lookup_populated`,
`test_mismatched_binding_fires`,
`test_envelope_absence_attribution_is_report_only`,
`test_reconcile_end_to_end_envelopes_flag`,
`test_presence_check_removal_is_silent` (restore half); the 6 quiet pins
hold. NOTE (minor doc imprecision, see Finding F2): the log's
parenthetical names "both end-to-end flag tests" among the five; observed
is ONE end-to-end flag test plus the attribution report-only pin (the
matching-envelope-quiet e2e test correctly holds as a quiet pin). Count
(5) and signature (clean-no-envelope returns to silent) reproduce exactly.

Worktree untouched: sabotage existed only at
`/tmp/f4qa-r1/scripts/reconcile_model.py:1092`.

