## Judge answers

(a) V33 absence is RIGHT. Per `design.md` §5, V33 appends only if a
sabotage restores silence while the corpus stays green. Q-R1, Q-R2/Q-R2b,
Q-R3 each flip named pins RED with GREEN on pristine files; no
silence-with-green-corpus direction exists. `verify-rigs.sh` correctly
stays at 39/0 with V31 last and V1–V31 unrenumbered.
(b) Default-empty lookup preserves clean-quiet in ALL CLI paths
(verified on pristine `reconcile.py` with the Q-R2 fixture):
`{}` envelopes file → exit 0 in sync; no `--envelopes` flag → exit 0;
non-dict envelopes file → exit 2 `UNPARSEABLE ENVELOPES (expected a JSON
object)` fail-closed; matching envelope → exit 0. `if not
envelope_by_id: return None` covers both `None` and `{}` at the single
gate; no path bypasses it (the clean-landing tail is the only caller).
(c) Report accuracy: all command/output claims re-verified above EXCEPT
two minor notes recorded as Findings F1 (secret-sweep `⇒ empty`
overstates the literal grep output — substance holds, see F1) and F2
(R1 parenthetical mislabels one of the five failing pins — count and
signature exact).

## Findings

F1 (MINOR, informational — not a FAIL): implementation report §Validation
claims `grep -rE '[A-Za-z0-9_-]{40,}' docs/evidence/f4-amendment/ ⇒
empty`; the literal command returns 4 hits (3 sha256 restore pins +
1 long test identifier). Substance holds: the three 64-hex strings are
one-way digests of committed public source files (independently
re-verified by QA: `sha256sum` of all three files matches the log pins
exactly — corroborating the byte-identical restore claims), the fourth
is a test-method name; no bearer material, fixtures stay dummy/16-hex.
Recommend rewording to "no secret-shaped bearer material (only sha256
restore pins + long identifiers)".
F2 (MINOR, informational — not a FAIL): `red-proofs.log` R1
parenthetical lists "both end-to-end flag tests" among the 5 failures;
QA-observed 5th-set member is the attribution report-only pin (the
second e2e test is a quiet pin and correctly holds). Count (5),
signature, and restore behavior reproduce exactly; enumeration only.

No FAIL-grade findings. No vacuous checks (every acceptance check was
forced RED by a minimal targeted sabotage and restored GREEN).
Worktree left clean: `git status --short` empty; nothing committed.
